{"id":13490029102746,"type":"album","name":"The Argument","artist":"Fugazi","year":2001,"weight":14,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/1144-the-argument_143131.jpg","aoty":85,"aoty_user":84,"yt":"yFyzhyBA7To","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/fugazi/the-argument","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/1144-fugazi-the-argument.php"},"desc":"The Argument is the sixth and most recent studio album from Fugazi released on October 16, 2001, through Dischord Records. It was recorded at Don Zientara's Inner Ear Studios in Arlington, VA and the Dischord House between January and April 2001. It was the band's last release (simultaneously with the Furniture EP) before going on hiatus in 2003. The Argument saw Fugazi continue to expand upon the more experimental art punk leanings of Red Medicine and End Hits while also heavily incorporating other instruments, such as piano and cello into their sound.The album also featured the first extensive contributions from ."},"artist_ref":{"id":222418642650593,"name":"Fugazi","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/FUGAZI_3_%2819729214472%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":165379782273035,"type":"genre","name":"Hardcore [Punk]","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":714,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":237890000566646,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Hardcore","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":341,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":15546028624161,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Post-Hardcore","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":7,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi